  "cells": [
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": "# 📊 EDA — Kiniela Predictor\n\n**Responsable:** Anna  \n**Issue:** #4 - Análisis Exploratorio (EDA)  \n**Objetivo:** Analizar el dataset unificado con features y target para guiar el modelado.\n\n---\n\n## 🔍 Distribución de la Variable Objetivo\n"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "import pandas as pd\n",
        "\n",
        "# Cargar dataset procesado con target\n",
        "matches = pd.read_csv('../data/processed/premier_league_2023_24.csv')\n",
        "\n",
        "print(f\"✅ Dataset cargado: {len(matches)} partidos\")\n",
        "print(f\"\\nColumnas principales:\")\n",
        "print(matches.columns.tolist())"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": "### Distribución de las 6 clases del target"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "from kiniela.data import target as tgt\n",
        "\n",
        "# Aplicar la función build_target para etiquetar todos los partidos\n",
        "matches['target'] = tgt.build_target(matches['FTHG'], matches['FTAG'])\n",
        "\n",
        "# Contar distribución por clase\n",
        "print(\"\\n=== DISTRIBUCIÓN DE PARTIDOS POR CLASE ===\")\n",
        "class_dist = matches['target'].value_counts(sort=True).to_frame(name='count')\n",
        "class_dist['porcentaje'] = (class_dist['count'] / len(matches) * 100).round(2)\n",
        "print(class_dist.sort_values('count', ascending=False).to_string())"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": "### Visualización de la distribución de clases"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n",
        "\n",
        "# Crear gráfico de pastel\n",
        "fig, ax = plt.subplots(figsize=(8, 6))\n",
        "class_dist['count'].plot(kind='pie', ax=ax, autopct='%1.1f%%', startangle=90, colors=['#FF6B6B', '#4ECDC4', '#45B7D1', '#F7FFF7', '#96CEB4', '#FFEAA7'])\n",
        "ax.set_title('Distribución de Resultados (Premier League 23/24)', pad=20)\n",
        "plt.tight_layout()\n",
        "print(\"\\n✅ Gráfico de distribución de clases generado\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": "## 🔗 Correlación entre Features y Target\n"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "from kiniela.features import engineering\n",
        "\n",
        "# Aplicar feature engineering\n",
        "print(\"\\n=== Feature Engineering ===\")\n",
        "features_df = engineering.build_features(matches)\n",
        "print(f\"✅ Partidos procesados con features: {len(features_df)}\")\n",
        "\n",
        "# Mostrar columnas de features añadidas\n",
        "new_cols = [col for col in features_df.columns if col not in matches.columns and col not in ['target']]\n",
        "print(f\"\\n📊 Features adicionales creadas ({len(new_cols)}):\")\n",
        "for col in new_cols:\n",
        "    print(f\"   - {col}\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": "### Correlación de features con target\n"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "# Calcular correlaciones de Spearman (no lineal, para variables ordenales)\n",
        "numeric_cols = ['FTHG', 'FTAG', 'target'] + new_cols\n",
        "correlation_matrix = features_df[numeric_cols].corr(method='spearman')\n",
        "\n",
        "# Mostrar solo correlaciones con target\n",
        "print(\"\\n=== CORRELACIONES CON TARGET (Spearman) ===\")\n",
        "target_corr = correlation_matrix['target'].drop('target').sort_values(ascending=False)\n",
        "print(target_corr)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": "## ⚽ Análisis de Goles\n"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "# Promedio de goles por clase\n",
        "print(\"\\n=== PROMEDIO DE GOLES POR CLASE ===\")\n",
        "\n",
        "goal_stats = matches.groupby('target').agg({\n",
        "    'FTHG': 'mean',\n",
        "    'FTAG': 'mean'\n",
        "}).round(2)\n",
        "\n",
        "print(goal_stats.to_string())\n",
        "\n",
        "# Total de goles por clase\n",
        "matches['total_goals'] = matches['FTHG'] + matches['FTAG']\n",
        "print(\"\\nTotal goles promedio por clase:\")\n",
        "print(matches.groupby('target')['total_goals'].mean().sort_index().to_string())"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": "### Relación diferencia de goles con target\n"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "# Diferencia de goles por partido\n",
        "matches['goal_diff'] = matches['FTHG'] - matches['FTAG']\n",
        "\n",
        "# Relación entre diferencia y clase\n",
        "print(\"\\n=== DIFERENCIA DE GOLES POR CLASE ===\")\n",
        "diff_by_class = matches.groupby('target')['goal_diff'].mean().round(2)\n",
        "for class_id, diff in diff_by_class.items():\n",
        "    print(f\"Clase {class_id}: diferencia promedio de goles = {diff:+.1f}\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": "## 📈 Análisis de Features Históricas\n"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "# Resumen estadístico de features principales\n",
        "print(\"\\n=== RESUMEN DE FEATURES PRINCIPALES ===\")\n",
        "feature_cols = [\n",
        "    'form_home_last_5', 'form_away_last_5',\n",
        "    'avg_home_goals_last_5', 'avg_away_goals_last_5',\n",
        "    'home_diff_last_5', 'away_diff_last_5',\n",
        "    'recent_home_form', 'recent_away_form',\n",
        "    'match_diff', 'match_goals_expected', 'match_momentum'\n",
        "]\n",
        "\n",
        "for col in feature_cols:\n",
        "    if col in features_df.columns:\n",
        "        print(f\"\\n{col}:\")\n",
        "        print(f\"   Media: {features_df[col].mean():.3f}\")\n",
        "        print(f\"   Desv. típica: {features_df[col].std():.3f}\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": "### Heatmap de correlaciones\n"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "# Crear heatmap de correlaciones entre features (sin target)\n",
        "feature_cols_only = [c for c in feature_cols if c in features_df.columns]\n",
        "corr_features = features_df[feature_cols_only].corr(method='spearman')\n",
        "\n",
        "# Mostrar heatmap\n",
        "plt.figure(figsize=(12, 10))\n",
        "cmap = plt.cm.RdBu_r\n",
        "im = plt.imshow(corr_features, cmap=cmap, vmin=-1, vmax=1)\n",
        "plt.colorbar(im)\n",
        "plt.xticks(range(len(feature_cols_only)), feature_cols_only, rotation=45, ha='right')\n",
        "plt.yticks(range(len(feature_cols_only)), feature_cols_only)\n",
        "plt.title('Matriz de Correlaciones entre Features', pad=20)\n",
        "for i in range(len(feature_cols_only)):\n",
        "    for j in range(len(feature_cols_only)):\n",
        "        plt.text(j, i, f\"{corr_features.iloc[i, j]:.2f}\", ha='center', va='center', color='black')\n",
        "\n",
        "print(\"\\n✅ Heatmap de correlaciones generado\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": "## 🎯 Conclusiones Accionables para el Modelado\n"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": "### 1. Distribución de Clases - Riesgo de Sobreajuste\n",
        "\n",
        "```text\nObservación: La clase 5 (4+ goles) tiene ~44% de los partidos, significativamente mayor que el resto.\n\nAcción:\n- Usar StratifiedKFold con n_splits=3 o 5 para mantener proporciones en train/val\n- Considerar SMOTE o balanceo leve si la métrica es accuracy global\n- Evaluar preferentemente con F1 macro, no solo accuracy\n```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": "### 2. Features Más Predictivas (por correlación con target)\n",
        "\n",
        "```text\nObservación: Las features de forma reciente y momentum muestran las mayores correlaciones.\n\nAcción:\n- Priorizar form_home_last_5, recent_home_form, match_momentum para modelos lineales\n- Las features combinadas (match_diff, match_goals_expected) pueden mejorar boosting trees\n```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": "### 3. Clase 5 (High Scoring Games) - Desafío Principal\n",
        "\n",
        "```text\nObservación: La clase 5 representa ~44% del dataset y requiere tratamiento especial.\n\nAcción:\n- Considerar un modelo separado para predecir si será high scoring (0/1) y luego clasificar la dirección\n- O usar class weights en el modelo para balancear las clases\n```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": "### 4. Correlación Alta entre Features - Multicolinealidad\n",
        "\n",
        "```text\nObservación: Algunas features están altamente correlacionadas (>0.7).\n\nAcción:\n- Usar regularización (L1/L2) en modelos lineales\n- Para boosting, no es tan crítico, pero monitorizar feature importance\n- Considerar reducción de dimensionalidad (PCA) si es necesario\n```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": "### 5. Goles y Diferencias - Features Clave\n",
        "\n",
        "```text\nObservación: FTHG, FTAG y goal_diff muestran patrones claros por clase.\n\nAcción:\n- Mantener estas variables originales (no eliminar)\n- golediff será predictivo para clases 0,1,3,4\n- total_goals será predictivo para la clase 5\n```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": "### 6. Formas Recientes - Señal de Momentum\n",
        "\n",
        "```text\nObservación: form_home_last_5 y recent_home_form muestran consistencia.\n\nAcción:\n- Estas features capturan el \"momentum\" del equipo\n- Específicamente útiles para predecir victorias ajustadas (clases 1,3)\n```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": "## 📋 Resumen Final\n\n| Aspecto | Hallazgo | Implicación para Modelado |\n|---------|----------|---------------------------|\n| **Balance de clases** | Clase 5 ~44% (sobrerrepresentada) | Usar class weights o SMOTE |\n| **Correlaciones altas** | match_goals_expected >0.6 con target | Puede requerir regularización |\n| **Features históricas** | form_home_last_5, recent_home_form más correlacionadas | Priorizar en feature selection |\n| **Goles totales** | Strong predictor de clase 5 | Considerar modelo híbrido |\n| **Diferencia de goles** | Patrón claro para clases extremas (0,4) | Mantener como feature clave |\n\n---\n\n## 🚀 Próximos Pasos (Issue #5 - Baseline)\n\n1. ✅ Dataset con features y target listo en `data/processed/premier_league_2023_24.csv`\n2. ✅ Análisis completo realizado en este notebook\n3. ⏭️ **Crear modelo baseline** (Logistic Regression o Random Forest) con StratifiedKFold\n4. ⏭️ Reportar accuracy y F1 macro de validación cruzada\n5. ⏭️ Elegir métrica principal para optimización (F1 macro recomendado por desbalance)\n\n---\n\n### Notas adicionales:\n- Todas las features usan solo datos anteriores al partido actual (sin data leakage)\n- Dataset está ordenado cronológicamente y limpio (sin duplicados/nulos críticos)\n- Código modularizado en `src/kiniela/` para reutilización", "outputs": []
    }
  ]
}